{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtIrreducible"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.dominance_of_tableau_noclash","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.dominance_of_tableau_noclash","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L169-L194","doc":"**Sagan Lemma 2.2.6, for tableaux.** `t` of shape `μ` and `s` of shape `ν`\non the same labels (via `h`): if no column of `t` meets a row of `s` twice, then\n`μ` dominates `ν`.\n\nThe conclusion is definitionally `SpechtClassification.partitionDom μ ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.colPattern_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.colPattern_mem","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L164-L167","doc":"Every label of a tableau sits in a column of `μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.rowPattern_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.rowPattern_card","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L155-L162","doc":"The labels of a tableau in the first `r` rows number `Σ_{j<r} μ_j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.colPattern_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.colPattern_card","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L149-L153","doc":"The labels of a tableau in column `c` number `μ.colLen c` — `Col_card`,\nrenamed for symmetry with `rowPattern_card`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.dominance_of_noclash","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.dominance_of_noclash","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L81-L143","doc":"**Sagan Lemma 2.2.6 (abstract form).**\n\n`ct` is the column pattern of a `μ`-tableau, `rs` the row pattern of a\n`ν`-tableau, both on the same `n` labels. If no two labels share both a column\nunder `ct` and a row under `rs`, then `μ ⊵ ν`.\n\nThe conclusion is stated as the raw partial-sum inequality, which is\ndefinitionally `SpechtClassification.partitionDom μ ν`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.card_cells_row_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtCrossDominance.card_cells_row_lt","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtCrossDominance.lean#L56-L73","doc":"The number of labels in the first `r` rows, read off the cells: it is the\npartial sum of row lengths. ","signatureChunk":0}]}